id: pm-vcs-dzz3
title: Review state as a record that merges per field
description: "Review state is a record that merges per field so two reviewers writing different fields concurrently never conflict. Prove it by merging two real branches that both wrote review state, asserting both survive, and that a genuinely conflicting single field is still reported as a conflict."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-28T13:43:07.406Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T15:48:57.219Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T15:48:57.202Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T15:48:57.202Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-5h6j,parent,"2026-08-28T15:22:35.562Z",claude,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T15:37:37.458Z",claude,"The per-field merge is proven against two real branches rather than a simulated merge: two reviewers writing different fields of one review record both survive, a reviewers-set addition from each side survives, and a genuinely conflicting scalar is still reported as a conflict while the other fields merge. approved_at is treated as a timestamp that converges to the latest, and createReviewRecord omits absent optional fields so an unset field does not merge as a deletion."
